        <title>AVM Updates</title>
        <description>Update feed for AVM, the Accessible Virtual Machine. Entries are added here with each release.</description>
        <language>en</language>
        <!-- Releases of this fork are added here, newest first. Each needs an
             enclosure signed with this fork's own EdDSA key (Sparkle's
             sign_update), matching SUPublicEDKey in AVM/Info.plist. The
             original project's releases are not listed: they are built for
             its own app and could not be installed over this one. -->
        <item>
            <title>Version 0.4.18</title>
            <sparkle:version>38</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.18</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul><li>AVM speaks in VoiceOver again while you&#x27;re in other apps. In 0.4.17 every line there failed and the system voice took over until AVM quit.</li><li>The Permissions window now sees VoiceOver Utility&#x27;s Allow VoiceOver to be controlled with AppleScript when it&#x27;s on, and says whether that switch or AVM&#x27;s Automation permission is the one still missing.</li><li>Download Windows works in the setup wizard: the installer AVM makes from Microsoft&#x27;s download is no longer called unreadable.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:28:51 +0000</pubDate>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/amenathomas1997/accessible-virtual-machine/releases/download/v0.4.18/AVM-0.4.18.zip" sparkle:edSignature="drzNBGl87CKTxb3z05sFJsGngeCVypZmmAE4KLt5MBZkAH0SoXG0MheTBdT72hgXbEqRLOHu8YIn3x/7hL1KBg==" length="67707213" type="application/octet-stream" />
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>Version 0.4.17</title>
            <sparkle:version>37</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.17</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul><li>New macOS machines can set themselves up: turn on Set up macOS for me in New macOS Virtual Machine, give your name and a password, and AVM goes through Setup Assistant, signs in, and turns on VoiceOver. If a screen stops it, AVM reads that screen to you.</li><li>A Permissions window, in the AVM menu, lists everything macOS has to allow for AVM, what each is for, and a button to allow it. It opens by itself only when something you use isn&#x27;t allowed.</li><li>When AVM opens at login, only the machine that starts shows. AVM&#x27;s own window stays away until you open AVM from the Dock or Applications.</li><li>If no keyboard is chosen for Windows when a Windows machine starts, AVM offers the second keyboard it finds.</li><li>Virtual Machine menu: Type Clipboard (Command-Shift-V) types what you copied into Windows, Read Screen (Command-Shift-O) reads out the text on a machine&#x27;s screen, and Speak Updates and Disk (Command-Option-Shift-I) says the free disk space and pending updates in Windows or Linux.</li><li>A machine&#x27;s Sound settings can send its sound to any output device, such as headphones or a hearing aid, instead of the Mac&#x27;s own.</li><li>Report a Problem can email the whole log, and the AVM menu has Remove AVM, which takes AVM, its USB helper and its settings off your Mac.</li><li>A saved macOS machine started while the Mac is locked now resumes when you unlock it, instead of starting afresh and losing where you were.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:05:41 +0000</pubDate>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/amenathomas1997/accessible-virtual-machine/releases/download/v0.4.17/AVM-0.4.17.zip" sparkle:edSignature="KlLK0k68hg2UdOR8dLtabKF0KSuLcUM1t2MAblGDi/GTBEf7PNAPkaSaLsXkFl0rw9i0GqLmGTNkt4Tt+PCkBQ==" length="67703696" type="application/octet-stream" />
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>Version 0.4.16</title>
            <sparkle:version>36</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.16</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul><li>Each virtual machine&#x27;s name is a heading in the dashboard&#x27;s table, so VO-Command-H goes from machine to machine. The table also says Memory and Disk in gigabytes.</li><li>A machine&#x27;s Settings come in five categories: General, Sharing, Devices, Display and Sound, and Startup and Recovery. Choose one in the Categories toolbar at the top, or with Command-1 to Command-5.</li><li>The setup wizard can download Linux: Download Linux gets Ubuntu Desktop, Debian or Fedora, checks it, and chooses it as the installer.</li><li>Each machine&#x27;s Settings can leave it out of Command-Tab.</li><li>AVM comes to the front whenever it starts a machine that takes your keyboard, so the keyboard goes in and AVM stays in Command-Tab.</li><li>A new Ubuntu machine has the guest agent, so AVM can shut it down and send it files. Machines made earlier don&#x27;t: install qemu-guest-agent in Ubuntu once.</li><li>The setup wizard downloads Windows 11 for ARM itself, straight from Microsoft, in your Mac&#x27;s language: no web page to use. It checks the download and makes it into the installer.</li><li>Installing Windows no longer stops for good when an installer hangs during setup, as the one Microsoft&#x27;s download gives did. Anything that didn&#x27;t finish installs when you first sign in.</li><li>When AVM opens at login and starts a machine, the list of machines opens too, behind it, so the other machines and AVM&#x27;s settings are a window away.</li><li>AVM has Settings of its own: Command-Comma from any AVM window. General has updates and What&#x27;s New, Startup and Background has opening at login and running in the background, Keyboard has Caps Lock as the screen reader key, and Devices has Restart USB Helper. A machine&#x27;s own Settings are now Command-Option-Comma.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:35:57 +0000</pubDate>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/amenathomas1997/accessible-virtual-machine/releases/download/v0.4.16/AVM-0.4.16.zip" sparkle:edSignature="infPfasVSvKVtUVJusJ2QgayzH46/VVpucdbkqKBvkod/ID31yj6lW/eoenhtPiZGPsURUJdekkhOBJiB17JCA==" length="67601678" type="application/octet-stream" />
        </item>
